From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:13:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 110/112] test: add feature_signet_slhblock.py

Two custom signets, each with nodes that have -signetslhblock and one that has
only -signetpqblock (with M4R_BITCOIND=<bitcoind>, a build without this series):

- an OP_TRUE challenge: the options (with negative, empty, zero and
  overflowing heights) and the startup log; below the height, the per-block
  verdicts; at the height, the negative list of the design through
  submitblock (the SLH output missing, after the commitment, at c - 2, c = 0;
  header PQB1 and PQH2, versions 0 and 2, OP_PUSHDATA4 and OP_PUSHDATA1,
  signatures of 7855 and 7857 bytes, a byte after it, amount 1, the prefix in
  other outputs, non-push and unparsable bytes; a flipped bit, another key,
  two wrong contexts, the wrong tag, an uncut message), each refused with
  bad-signet-slhblk and taken by the old node; a block made in the wrong order
  (ML-DSA-44 first, SLH second), refused by both with bad-signet-pqblk; more
  commitment-prefixed and OP_RETURN outputs, taken by both; a full template
  with -blockreservedweight=48000, which fits, and with 16000, which no longer
  does; -reindex-chainstate and -reindex; compact block relay of an SLH block
  between two nodes with the rule; a late upgrade;
- a 1-of-1 bare multisig challenge like Ark-0's: blocks made the way the
  Ark-0 producer makes them, with signet-slh-sign and the wallet's signet
  solution through contrib/signet/miner, and the wrong order again;

a node with Ark-0's challenge, which has no SLH-DSA block signature; the
p2mr-ts vectors of slh_msg; and, through submitblock on a node of its own,
the BIP34 heights of the design (127, 128, 255, 256, 32767, 32768,
8388607, 8388608 and INT_MAX - 1): the rule runs on the height the
coinbase commits to, before that height is compared with the block's, so
a block at height 1 committing to h - 1 passes the rule at h (and fails
as bad-cb-height), one committing to h without the signature fails it,
and one with it passes; a non-minimal push of height 1 counts as reached;
and the genesis block, which submitblock passes through CheckBlock before
it answers "duplicate": with the rule from height 1 the answer is
"duplicate", where without the exemption it would be bad-signet-slhblk.
